export partinst="partitioning instructions:"
export partinst=$partinst"\\nTo create new partitions, type n at the command prompt. To change a partition's name after creation, type c."
export partinst=$partinst"\\ncreate at least 3 partitions. The following layout is suggested:"
export partinst=$partinst"\\npartition 1: from sector 0 to 2M, type code ef02, for BIOS Boot, name none"
export partinst=$partinst"\\npartition 2, from 2M to 502M, for uefi boot and linux kernel, type code ef00, name EFI"
export partinst=$partinst"\\npartition 3, from 502M to however large you want your linux installation to be, default type code 8300, name linux."
export partinst=$partinst"\\nfeel free to make changes to this suggested layout, but the type codes and partition names must be as stated in the instructions for a successful installation."
export partinst=$partinst"\\nif you made a mestake and want to start from scratch, type o, y, enter to destroy the in memory copy of the partition table. Don't forget to type w enter y enter to write your new partition table to the disk."
